    "long_instructions": "#### Think about the page you just built in Web Lab. Good digital displays don’t just look nice,  they also help users stay safe and understand information easily. \r\n\r\n## Helpful Tips about Data Safety\r\n\r\n#### These ideas can help you make thoughtful choices about what information to show, how to show it, and how to keep users safe when designing displays.\r\n\r\n<table style=\"width: 100%; border-collapse: collapse;\">\r\n  <tr>\r\n    <td style=\"vertical-align: top; width: 50%; padding: 5px;\">\r\n      <details style=\"background-color: #ececec; padding: 10px; margin-bottom: 10px; border: 1px solid transparent; border-radius: 5px;\">\r\n        <summary style=\"font-size: 1.2em; font-weight: bold;\">🔒 Data Minimization</summary>\r\n        <div style=\"margin-top: 10px; margin-left: 10px; margin-right: 10px; margin-bottom: 10px;\">\r\n          <p>Show only the information that is actually needed.<br>More data = more risk.</p>\r\n        </div>\r\n      </details>\r\n    </td>\r\n\r\n<td style=\"vertical-align: top; width: 50%; padding: 5px;\">\r\n      <details style=\"background-color: #ececec; padding: 10px; margin-bottom: 10px; border: 1px solid transparent; border-radius: 5px;\">\r\n        <summary style=\"font-size: 1.2em; font-weight: bold;\">🙈 Avoid Personal Identifiers</summary>\r\n        <div style=\"margin-top: 10px; margin-left: 10px; margin-right: 10px; margin-bottom: 10px;\">\r\n          <p>If the data is about a person, don’t include names, birthdays, locations, or anything that could identify someone unless absolutely necessary.</p>\r\n        </div>\r\n      </details>\r\n    </td>\r\n  </tr>\r\n\r\n  <tr>\r\n<td style=\"vertical-align: top; width: 50%; padding: 5px;\">\r\n      <details style=\"background-color: #ececec; padding: 10px; margin-bottom: 10px; border: 1px solid transparent; border-radius: 5px;\">\r\n        <summary style=\"font-size: 1.2em; font-weight: bold;\">🎯 Purposeful Display</summary>\r\n        <div style=\"margin-top: 10px; margin-left: 10px; margin-right: 10px; margin-bottom: 10px;\">\r\n          <p>Think about why each field is shown.<br>If a field doesn’t help the user make a decision, it might not need to be displayed.</p>\r\n        </div>\r\n      </details>\r\n    </td>\r\n\r\n<td style=\"vertical-align: top; width: 50%; padding: 5px;\">\r\n      <details style=\"background-color: #ececec; padding: 10px; margin-bottom: 10px; border: 1px solid transparent; border-radius: 5px;\">\r\n        <summary style=\"font-size: 1.2em; font-weight: bold;\">⚕️ Sensitive Information Needs Care</summary>\r\n        <div style=\"margin-top: 10px; margin-left: 10px; margin-right: 10px; margin-bottom: 10px;\">\r\n          <p>Some data (like medical info, allergies, or safety details) should be displayed clearly but respectfully, without extra unnecessary description.</p>\r\n        </div>\r\n      </details>\r\n    </td>\r\n  </tr>\r\n\r\n  <tr>\r\n<td style=\"vertical-align: top; width: 50%; padding: 5px;\">\r\n      <details style=\"background-color: #ececec; padding: 10px; margin-bottom: 10px; border: 1px solid transparent; border-radius: 5px;\">\r\n        <summary style=\"font-size: 1.2em; font-weight: bold;\">🗂️ Safe Grouping</summary>\r\n        <div style=\"margin-top: 10px; margin-left: 10px; margin-right: 10px; margin-bottom: 10px;\">\r\n          <p>Group related information so users can quickly understand it without digging through too much detail.</p>\r\n        </div>\r\n      </details>\r\n    </td>\r\n\r\n<td style=\"vertical-align: top; width: 50%; padding: 5px;\">\r\n      <details style=\"background-color: #ececec; padding: 10px; margin-bottom: 10px; border: 1px solid transparent; border-radius: 5px;\">\r\n        <summary style=\"font-size: 1.2em; font-weight: bold;\">👀 Clarity Helps Safety</summary>\r\n        <div style=\"margin-top: 10px; margin-left: 10px; margin-right: 10px; margin-bottom: 10px;\">\r\n          <p>Confusing displays can lead to mistakes — like misreading an allergy severity. Clear labeling and good layout actually help keep users safe.</p>\r\n        </div>\r\n      </details>\r\n    </td>\r\n  </tr>\r\n</table>\r\n\r\n\r\n--- \r\n#### Answer **one** of the questions below to reflect on how your design choices supported clarity, accessibility, and data safety.\r\n\r\n\r\n- #### What choices did you make about **which fields to show** and how to lay them out on the screen?\r\n- #### How do those choices help make the display **clear and accessible** for users? (You might mention labels, order, grouping, or readability.)\r\n- #### How did you protect users’ **privacy or safety** when deciding what **not** to show?",
